data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"\"content\": \"# Dispatch to qa — verify the Colour Greeting against DESIGN.md\\n\\nVerify the developer's application against the design, per your brief\\n(roles/qa.md). One pass, one report.\\n\\nI have pushed my HEAD into your clone at `refs/campaign/orchestrator`\\n(commit 871270f). It holds both `DESIGN.md` and the developer's application.\\nCheck it out with:\\n\\n    git checkout refs/campaign/orchestrator\\n\\nThen, per your brief:\\n\\n1. Read `DESIGN.md` first — it is the standard you verify against.\\n2. Run the documented build command (`npm run build`) and the documented serve\\n   command (`npm run serve`). Note: `npm run serve` is `vite preview`, which\\n   binds localhost on its own port (4173) — read the URL it prints. The\\n   production-facing dev server (`npm run dev`, bound to 0.0.0.0:5173) is\\n   already running on the orchestrator's machine; your job is verification of\\n   the build in your clone, on whatever address your serve command prints.\\n   You will need `npm install` first.\\n3. Check the interface against the design: the exact greeting `Hello, world!`;\\n   three buttons labelled Blue, Orange, Violet; clicking each changes the\\n   greeting's colour to `--color-cat-1`, `--color-cat-6`, `--color-cat-5`\\n   respectively; default on load is Blue; Header title \\\"Colour Greeting\\\" with\\n   no nav; Footer text \\\"Built with the codesweep design system\\\"; centred\\n   layout per the design.\\n4. Confirm real design-system use: `package.json` lists `@codesweep-ai/ui`;\\n   the rendered page shows that package's `Header`, `Footer` and `Button`\\n   (each renders a `data-component` attribute naming it — look for those in\\n   the served page); greeting colours come from its `--color-*` tokens (no\\n   hex values in the application source).\\n\\nReport what you ran and what you observed, and name how you measured it. Where\\na requirement fails, say so plainly and name the evidence. Do not fix the\\napplication — the developer owns that.\\n"},"index":0}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1793343338,"id":"chatcmpl-7fa00472","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

